  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.0\n- .NET Framework 4.x on Windows: launch and attach, legacy (non-SDK) projects built with MSBuild.exe, integratedTerminal/externalTerminal, several AppDomains, Windows (full/pdbonly) PDBs, NGen disabled with justMyCode=false.\n- 32-bit processes are refused with a plain message (64-bit only).\n- Linux/macOS, .NET 8: the adapter no longer hangs after \"The debuggee cannot be stopped\" while expanding an object.\n- Fixes from a black-box DAP probe of 0.1.0: unhandled exceptions always stop, non-ASCII output on Windows, async stepping, long strings, attach errors, paged and capped variables, implicit evaluation timeouts (option allowImplicitFuncEval), robust DAP parsing, expression evaluator additions.\n- JetBrains DAP client compatibility: variables filter \"named\", namedVariables, sorted threads, single terminate, exited -1 for a terminated debuggee.\nFull list: https://github.com/dvislobokov/dotnet-debugger/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
